## Purpose and Scope

This document explains how components dynamically generate input and output ports based on their configuration. Dynamic port resolution allows components to adapt their connectivity interface at runtime, enabling flexible workflow designs where port availability depends on parameter values.

For information about static component metadata and the component registry, see [Component Registry](#3.1). For details on how components execute with these ports, see [Component Execution Model](#3.2). For parameter configuration UI, see [Parameter Configuration](#3.3).

---

## Overview

Components in ShipSec Studio can define ports in two ways:

| Port Type | Definition | Resolution Timing | Use Cases |
|-----------|-----------|-------------------|-----------|
| **Static Ports** | Defined in component metadata (`inputs`, `outputs` fields) | At component registration | Fixed component interfaces (e.g., HTTP request always has `url` input and `response` output) |
| **Dynamic Ports** | Generated by component's `resolvePorts()` function | When parameters change or workflow loads | Parameter-driven interfaces (e.g., Entry Point creates outputs based on runtime input definitions) |

Dynamic ports enable components to:
- Create outputs that match user-defined runtime inputs (Entry Point)
- Generate inputs/outputs based on external tool discovery (MCP components)
- Adapt their interface based on configuration (e.g., toggling optional ports)

**Sources:** [backend/src/workflows/workflows.service.ts:385-467](), [frontend/src/components/workflow/ConfigPanel.tsx:442-508]()

