## Edge Management with Dynamic Ports

When dynamic ports change, the system must handle edges connected to removed ports.

### Canvas Edge Invalidation

The Canvas component removes edges when their source/target ports no longer exist:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Update Trigger"
        U["onUpdateNode(id, { dynamicOutputs })"]
    end

    subgraph "Validation"
        V1["Extract valid output IDs"]
        V2["Find edges from node"]
        V3["Check if sourceHandle in valid IDs"]
        V4["Mark edge for removal"]
    end

    subgraph "Cleanup"
        R1["Remove invalid edges"]
        R2["Clean up input mappings on target nodes"]
        R3["Update Canvas state"]
    end

    U --> V1
    V1 --> V2
    V2 --> V3
    V3 --> V4
    V4 --> R1
    R1 --> R2
    R2 --> R3
```

**Implementation details:**

```typescript
// Check for dynamic outputs change
const dynamicOutputs = (data as any).dynamicOutputs;
if (dynamicOutputs && Array.isArray(dynamicOutputs)) {
  const validOutputIds = new Set(dynamicOutputs.map((p: any) => p.id));

  // Find edges from this node that are now invalid
  updatedEdges.forEach((edge) => {
    if (edge.source === nodeId && 
        edge.sourceHandle && 
        !validOutputIds.has(edge.sourceHandle)) {
      edgesToRemove.push(edge);
    }
  });
}

// Similar logic for dynamicInputs
```

The same logic applies to `dynamicInputs` changes, removing edges to removed input ports.

**Sources:** [frontend/src/components/workflow/Canvas.tsx:762-826]()

### Input Mapping Cleanup

When an edge is removed due to port changes, the target node's input mapping must be cleaned:

```typescript
updatedNodes = updatedNodes.map((node) => {
  const incomingRemovedEdges = edgesToRemove.filter((e) => e.target === node.id);
  if (incomingRemovedEdges.length === 0) return node;

  const originalInputs = (node.data.inputs as Record<string, unknown>) || {};
  const keysToRemove = new Set(
    incomingRemovedEdges
      .filter((e) => e.targetHandle && originalInputs[e.targetHandle])
      .map((e) => e.targetHandle as string),
  );

  // Build new inputs object excluding removed keys
  const inputs = Object.fromEntries(
    Object.entries(originalInputs).filter(([key]) => !keysToRemove.has(key)),
  );

  return {
    ...node,
    data: { ...node.data, inputs },
  };
});
```

**Sources:** [frontend/src/components/workflow/Canvas.tsx:799-826]()

