This document describes how raw execution events are transformed into visual state objects that drive the Execution Inspector UI. The pipeline converts timestamped event streams into normalized timeline data structures (`TimelineEvent`, `NodeVisualState`, `DataPacket`) that can be efficiently rendered and animated.

For information about how events arrive via SSE and the live/replay modes, see page 5.2 (Live Execution Updates). For details on specific event types, see page 5.4 (Trace Events and Logs).

