## Log Mode Management

The execution store manages three distinct log modes to optimize data loading:

| Mode | Data Source | Use Case |
|------|-------------|----------|
| `live` | `liveLogs[]` from SSE | Real-time log tailing during execution |
| `historical` | `historicalLogs[]` from API | Complete logs for completed runs |
| `scrubbing` | `scrubberLogs[]` from time-range query | Logs for specific timeline position |

**Mode Switching Logic:**

```typescript
// Switch based on timeline playback mode
useEffect(() => {
  if (playbackMode === 'live') {
    setLogMode('live');
  } else if (playbackMode === 'replay') {
    setLogMode('historical');
  }
}, [playbackMode, setLogMode]);

// Get display logs based on current mode
const getDisplayLogs = () => {
  const state = get();
  switch (state.logMode) {
    case 'live': return state.liveLogs;
    case 'scrubbing': return state.scrubberLogs;
    case 'historical': return state.historicalLogs;
    default: return [];
  }
};
```

This separation prevents memory bloat (live logs are append-only) while enabling efficient scrubbing during replay.

