## Error Handling and Reconnection

### SSE Error Recovery

When the SSE connection fails, the store automatically attempts to reconnect using stored cursors:

```typescript
source.onerror = (event) => {
  console.warn('Execution stream error', event);
  source.close();
  set({ eventSource: null, streamingMode: 'none' });

  // monitorRun will attempt reconnection on next poll cycle
};
```

The polling interval (2 seconds) acts as a fallback to ensure status updates continue even during SSE outages.

### Graceful Degradation

When SSE is unavailable (old browsers, network restrictions), the system falls back to polling-only mode:

```typescript
// Backend signals connection mode
source.addEventListener('ready', (event) => {
  const payload = JSON.parse(event.data);
  set({ streamingMode: payload.mode }); // 'realtime' or 'polling'

  if (payload.mode === 'realtime') {
    // Reduce polling frequency as backup
    const backupPoll = setInterval(pollOnce, 5000);
  } else {
    // Maintain normal polling interval
  }
});
```

