This document describes the terminal output streaming system, which captures and displays real-time console output (stdout/stderr) and pseudo-terminal (PTY) sessions from component executions. For general execution monitoring concepts, see [Execution Monitoring](#5). For trace events and structured logs, see [Trace Events and Logs](#5.4).

Terminal streaming enables live viewing of component execution output (such as CLI tool output, script execution logs, or containerized process streams) with millisecond-precision timing information and support for replay at any point in the execution timeline.

---

## System Architecture

The terminal streaming system operates through four layers: collection in components, buffering in Redis, delivery via SSE, and display in the frontend.

