### Relation to Node I/O

Node I/O inspection ([see Node I/O Inspection](#5.6)) captures structured input/output data, while terminal streaming captures unstructured console output. They complement each other for different debugging scenarios:

- **Terminal:** "What did the script print?"
- **Node I/O:** "What data flowed between nodes?"

