### File Upload

File uploads use `FormData` with automatic `Content-Type` handling:

```typescript
upload: async (file: File) => {
  const response = (await apiClient.uploadFile(file)) as any;
  if (response.error) {
    const errorMessage =
      response.error instanceof Error
        ? response.error.message
        : typeof response.error === 'string'
          ? response.error
          : 'Failed to upload file';
    throw new Error(errorMessage);
  }
  return response.data;
}
```

The `ShipSecApiClient.uploadFile()` method converts the file to `FormData`:

```typescript
async uploadFile(file: File) {
  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('file', file);

  return this.client.POST('/api/v1/files/upload', {
    body: formData as any,
  });
}
```

**Sources:** [frontend/src/services/api.ts:963-975](), [packages/backend-client/src/api-client.ts:370-379]()

### Blob Downloads

Artifact and file downloads request blob responses and handle them specially:

```typescript
download: async (id: string): Promise<Blob> => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const response = await fetch(`${API_V1_URL}/artifacts/${id}/download`, {
    headers,
  });
  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error('Failed to download artifact');
  }
  return await response.blob();
}
```

For the typed client, blobs are requested using `parseAs: 'blob'`:

```typescript
async downloadFile(id: string): Promise<Blob> {
  const response = await this.client.GET('/api/v1/files/{id}/download', {
    params: { path: { id } },
    parseAs: 'blob',
  }) as any;

  if (response?.error) {
    throw new Error(`Failed to download file: ${String(response.error)}`);
  }

  return (response?.data ?? response) as Blob;
}
```

