## Data Spilling in Activities

Activities implement automatic data spilling to handle payloads that exceed Temporal's 2MB limit (`TEMPORAL_SPILL_THRESHOLD_BYTES`). This is critical for workflows that process large datasets or binary files.

### Spilling Process

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Workflow
    participant Activity
    participant Storage as MinIO
    participant Registry as Spilled Cache

    Workflow->>Activity: inputs with __spilled__ marker
    Activity->>Registry: Check cache

    alt Cache hit
        Registry-->>Activity: Return cached data
    else Cache miss
        Activity->>Storage: downloadFile(storageRef)
        Storage-->>Activity: Full data
        Activity->>Registry: Cache result
    end

    Activity->>Activity: Extract handle field
    Activity->>Activity: Execute component
    Activity->>Activity: Check output size

    alt Size > threshold
        Activity->>Storage: uploadFile(uuid, output)
        Activity-->>Workflow: Spilled marker
    else Size acceptable
        Activity-->>Workflow: Raw output
    end
```

**Spilled Data Marker Structure:**

```typescript
{
  __spilled__: true,
  storageRef: string,        // MinIO file ID
  __spilled_handle__: string, // Field path to extract
  originalSize: number
}
```

