## Activity Retry Policies

Activities support component-level retry policies defined in the workflow definition. The `mapRetryPolicy` function translates the `ComponentRetryPolicy` schema into Temporal's retry options:

```typescript
function mapRetryPolicy(policy?: ComponentRetryPolicy) {
  if (!policy) return undefined;

  return {
    maximumAttempts: policy.maxAttempts,
    initialInterval: policy.initialIntervalSeconds * 1000,
    maximumInterval: policy.maximumIntervalSeconds * 1000,
    backoffCoefficient: policy.backoffCoefficient,
    nonRetryableErrorTypes: policy.nonRetryableErrorTypes,
  };
}
```

The workflow applies these retry options when creating the activity proxy:

```typescript
const { runComponentActivity: runComponentWithRetry } = proxyActivities<{...}>({
  startToCloseTimeout: '10 minutes',
  retry: mapRetryPolicy(action.retryPolicy),
});
```

**Sources:** [worker/src/temporal/workflows/index.ts:140-154](), [worker/src/temporal/workflows/index.ts:788-795]()

