## Pending Output Detection

Components that require human input return a special output structure with `pending: true`. The workflow orchestration detects this marker and initiates the human input flow.

### Pending Marker Structure

```typescript
// Output from component that requires human input
{
  pending: true,
  inputType: 'approval' | 'form' | 'selection' | 'review' | 'acknowledge',
  title: string,
  description?: string,
  timeoutAt?: string,  // ISO timestamp

  // Type-specific fields:
  options?: Array<{id: string, label: string}>,  // For 'selection' type
  schema?: Record<string, unknown>,              // For 'form' type
  multiple?: boolean,                            // For 'selection' type
  contextData?: Record<string, unknown>          // Additional context
}
```

The `isApprovalPending()` function checks for this structure:

```typescript
function isApprovalPending(output: unknown): output is {
  pending: true; 
  title: string; 
  description?: string; 
  timeoutAt?: string 
} {
  return (
    typeof output === 'object' &&
    output !== null &&
    'pending' in output &&
    (output as { pending?: unknown }).pending === true
  );
}
```

**Sources:** [worker/src/temporal/workflows/index.ts:126-138](), [worker/src/temporal/workflows/index.ts:867-896]()

## Signal Handler Setup

The workflow sets up a signal handler at the beginning of execution to receive human input resolutions asynchronously:

```typescript
// Map tracking pending human inputs by nodeRef
const pendingHumanInputs = new Map<
  string,
  { nodeRef: string; resolve: (res: HumanInputResolution) => void }
>();

// Map storing completed resolutions
const humanInputResolutions = new Map<string, HumanInputResolution>();

// Signal handler registered once at workflow start
setHandler(resolveHumanInputSignal, (resolution: HumanInputResolution) => {
  console.log(
    `[Workflow] Received human input signal for ${resolution.nodeRef}: approved=${resolution.approved}`
  );
  humanInputResolutions.set(resolution.nodeRef, resolution);

  // Resolve any pending waiter
  const pending = pendingHumanInputs.get(resolution.nodeRef);
  if (pending) {
    pending.resolve(resolution);
  }
});
```

**Resolution structure:**
```typescript
interface HumanInputResolution {
  nodeRef: string;
  approved: boolean;
  respondedBy: string;
  responseNote?: string;
  responseData?: Record<string, unknown>;  // For forms/selections
  respondedAt: string;
}
```

**Sources:** [worker/src/temporal/workflows/index.ts:164-181]()

