## Component SDK Integration

Components that require human input use the execution context to check for and emit pending states. While the component itself doesn't directly handle the human input flow, it returns the pending marker that triggers the workflow-level handling:

```typescript
// Example component implementation (pseudocode)
export const manualApprovalComponent = {
  id: 'manual.approval',
  // ... other metadata

  execute: async ({ inputs, params }, context) => {
    const { title, description, timeoutSeconds } = params;

    // Component returns pending marker
    const timeoutAt = timeoutSeconds 
      ? new Date(Date.now() + timeoutSeconds * 1000).toISOString()
      : undefined;

    return {
      pending: true,
      inputType: 'approval',
      title,
      description,
      timeoutAt,
      contextData: inputs  // Pass context to display to user
    };
  }
};
```

The workflow orchestration layer detects the `pending: true` marker and handles all the signal/wait logic transparently.

